Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory, retrieved from that tag).
Copyright contributors to the vLLM project. The patch changes five files
(listed in patch/patch-manifest.json). As required by section 4(b) of the
Apache License 2.0, each changed file carries a prominent notice, added by the
patch directly below its original SPDX/Apache-2.0 header (which is retained
unchanged):

    # Modified by Serendipity One Inc., 2026: native decision readout (see serving/vllm/NOTICE).

The modifications add a native final-position candidate readout
(prefill-only scoring) to the completions endpoint, sampling parameters,
scheduler and GPU model runner. Files produced by common/build_overlay.py are
likewise derived from vLLM, carry the same notice and remain under Apache-2.0.
Do not redistribute patched vLLM files without this notice.

The remaining Python files in this directory are part of this repository and
follow the repository license.
